{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3003","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3003","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3003\",\"parent_revision\":\"7169a6f46f2ffa23638f6c05d408a1abed18bd9738112f9dbe9210d941f60be0\",\"root_revision\":\"7169a6f46f2ffa23638f6c05d408a1abed18bd9738112f9dbe9210d941f60be0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nInvoking Skill(skill='dh:work-backlog-item', args='create -- ...') fails deterministically with: Shell command failed for pattern !`...`: [stderr] (eval):1: permission denied: ../.. This happens at skill LOAD time, before any argument parsing \u2014 reproduced identically across two invocations with completely different args content (one containing backticks, one not), which rules out the args text as the trigger.\\n\\nRoot cause location: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md line 9 contains the injection line: !`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"` \u2014 this is the harness's own bang-backtick substitution mechanism (see AGENTS.md SKILL.md string substitution section), executed by the Claude Code harness at skill-load time, not by the agent's own Bash tool.\\n\\nFalsification check performed: ran the same script directly via plain node invocation (node plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs) from the repo root \u2014 it succeeded immediately (exit 0, valid token emitted). This rules out the script's own logic (get-gate-token.mjs) as the cause; the failure is specific to the harness's bang-backtick substitution/execution layer when loading this particular SKILL.md, observed while running from a git worktree (.claude/worktrees/section-roundtrip-tests) of this repo.\\n\\nImpact: the documented MCP path (mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_add with gate_token) and the entire work-backlog-item skill are unusable from this context \u2014 every workflow that begins with Skill(skill='dh:work-backlog-item', ...) is blocked, forcing a fallback to the CLI path (uv run plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_cli.py backlog add) which bypasses the create/scope.md gate read that the skill's own documentation calls a MCP-only guarantee.\\n\\nSuggested investigation starting points (not verified as root cause, just leads): (1) whether ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} resolves incorrectly to a path requiring ../.. traversal when the skill is loaded from a worktree vs the main checkout, (2) whether the harness's sandboxed exec for bang-backtick lines enforces a directory allowlist that the worktree path falls outside of.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bug: work-backlog-item skill fails to load - gate-token bang-backtick line throws permission denied ../** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - encountered while creating backlog item #3001, 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3d7775c1ef16f060de213c2089ed583b3ff0d791ef5d206752c55e5a702e5ae4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgvZYA\"}"}